{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/218416-can-i-get-some-tips-for-creating-a-cult","id":218416,"title":"Can I get some Tips for Creating a Cult","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-04T12:57:14-07:00","id":218416,"title":"Can I get some Tips for Creating a Cult","content":"Hey guys I'm looking for tips on creating a cult. Anyone got some example cults I can use to try to figure out how to write up mine ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T05:40:45-07:00","id":223158,"title":"","content":"Hey <b>Basic</b>, <br /> <br /> I don't think there's any supplements out that elaborate on how to build a cult with the Cultists Merit from the Demon Core Book. However, I have a character that has dots in the Mystery Cult Initiation Merit though and there are rules for building your own Mystery Cult that looks like a great starting point to build any cult from. This is a rough summary but it goes something like this:<br /> <br /> Purpose: In a Mystery Cult the purpose just describes what they do and try to accomplish. For the Cultist Merit it should somehow be a benefit to your Demon character. For instance a 2 dot Cultist's Purpose would be a very loose purpose since they can be called upon once per chapter to grant the Demon a boon similar to Allies, Contact, or Resources 3.<br /> <br /> Relic: Mystery Cults have some kind of artifact that serves as the focal point of the cult. It's always something eldritch and mysterious and's used mostly to help establish theme and to serve as a motivator for the cult's Purpose or Doctrine. For the Cultist Merit rather than a Relic the symbol of veneration is the Demon themselves, even though the cultists might not truly know who or what they are. An example of this would be if a demonic cult venerated a creature known as the Crimson Maiden and was run by the Demon's Cover. The iconography would be of the Demon's true form and any visible Embeds, Exploits, Gadgets, or partial transformations would be interpreted by the cultists as &quot;Gifts of the Crimson Maiden&quot; and only be available to the chosen of their deity, the Demon and perhaps her Ringmates.<br /> <br /> Doctrine: This is just the religion/rules for people in the cult. Since Demon's create their own cults the Doctrine is more of the laws the Demon sets down so that their cult adheres to the goals or beliefs the Demon approves of. This is a particularly tricky thing to do for low dot Cults since devotion to the cult's Doctrine might not be as important as a 5 dot Cults, where mortal worshipers view soul pacts as the highest honor imaginable. Using the example from above in the cult dedicated to the Crimson Maiden perhaps the cultist's Doctrine simply states that true believers in the Lady of Blood cannot let sin go unpunished. That way the Demon who formed it, a Saboteur who views the God Machine's callous nature as the root of all evil, will ensure that only those dedicated to punishing wrongdoers or those with strong violent streaks will be administered into her cult, ensuring that she'll have an army she can be proud of.<br /> <br /> Example Cult: <b>Keeper's of the Rift (Cultists 4)</b><br /> <br /> Purpose: The Keeper's of the Rift unknowingly hide and guard a Suborned Infrastructure for their hidden mistress, the Demon Shanaolot. Originally a group of scientists who accidentally uncovered a &quot;rift in space-time&quot; and were contacted by a pan-dimensional being who was trapped there, who in truth was an Angel that was assigned to eliminate a faulty Infrastructure who Fell when it accidentally got trapped and abandoned by it's creator, and granted forms of science and technology never before imagined, Embeds and Gadgets. The Keepers have watched over Shanaolot's domain for almost a decade now and have reaped great benefit from their mistress understanding of pan-dimensional science. It hasn't been easy though, for the cultist have had to compromise more of their humanity than they'd like to admit to keep the rift a secret. Higher truths have a steep cost after all, one drenched in the blood of both the enemy and the innocent.<br /> <br /> Deity: Shanaolot, She of the Barren Realm. Lady of a broken world that never was who contemplates the higher truths of the universe whilst avoiding re-imprisonment by her own creator. She has chosen those with the capacity to understand to aid her in her never ending quest to grasp the final truth of the universe, and transcend it's bounds forever. <br /> <br /> Doctrine: Knowledge is power. The enlightened seeker of knowledge is a pilgrim on a journey to the holy lands, for knowledge and understanding are spiritual nectar for the human soul. Beware those who act in ignorance, for knowing or not they are brigands and thieves who prey upon the enlightened pilgrim. They must not be shown mercy, for in their blindness they threaten the sanctity of the human soul itself. Those who walk the path of enlightenment must be steadfast in their journey. Always looking toward the distant horizon and higher truth.<br /> <br /> Hope this helps. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T16:14:36-07:00","id":223690,"title":"","content":"I adore that Merit. I use GMC in Mummy, and use that merit to buff mummy and demon cultists. However, personally i dont let the mummy have the merit, as they have the actual Cult merit. Id probably do it that way for demons, too, as their cult merit shows how they benefit, while the initiation one shows the cool reasons for humans to join that cult. Either way, that merit is an awesome way to customize a cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T10:15:06-07:00","id":224248,"title":"","content":"Should check out Antagonists and their stuff on Cults.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T11:19:32-07:00","id":227160,"title":"","content":"<b>Cleverest of Things</b>,<br /> <br /> I've found to much delight that the Mystery Cult Initiation Merit works great for Demons if it's used as one of their Cover Merits. That way it's more of another one of the many ways Demons can worm they're way into human institutions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}